 "narrative": "All returned estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction. For the negative-direction feature_045 claims, positive signed values mean the raw exposed-minus-comparator dependency score is more negative, i.e. feature_045=1 is associated with stronger dependency on outcome_006; for the positive-direction outcome_012 feature_034/feature_002 claims, positive signed values mean the raw contrast is in the asserted direction. No evidence supports accepting any claim outright at this stage. The most important negative result is that the H138 outcome_012 feature_034-by-feature_002 interaction does not survive decomposition. H165 in feature_002=1 is only +0.0123 with interval [-0.0104, 0.0351], and H166 in feature_002=0 is -0.0175 with interval [-0.0395, 0.0044]; both are clinically small under any reasonable mean-scale proxy and H166 is opposite the positive claim. The H138/H177 interaction point estimates are near the generous outcome_012 clinical proxy, but they are derived from opposite small subgroup contrasts rather than from large stratum-specific effects, and both discovery and validation intervals include zero and clinically smaller or opposite effects. Given the enormous multiplicity and the prior validation attenuation across the run, I reject and close H138 and the adjacent unvalidated H177 rather than accept a near-threshold interaction artifact. The null/low-support main-effect contexts H174 and H175 are also rejected and closed because they do not explain the interaction as a strong marginal baseline difference. The feature_045 block for outcome_006 is more internally coherent. The main effect H163 has a large positive signed point estimate, +0.0314, although the interval includes null and clinically smaller effects. The feature_002 stratum contrasts H167 and H168 and the feature_034 stratum contrasts H170 and H171 all point in the same stronger-dependency direction, while the interaction terms H169 and H172 are imprecise and null-compatible, which is more consistent with a main effect than with robust effect modification. However, this remains a post-screen subgroup decomposition with very wide intervals, and the pre-specified triangulation outcome_014 H173 is opposite in sign and null-compatible, so H163 cannot be accepted. I keep H163 active and request independent validation because it is the only remaining unvalidated candidate with both a high-magnitude point estimate and directional coherence across several balanced strata. H168 and H170 are the strongest supporting stratum contrasts and remain active pending validation, but they are not accepted. H173 is rejected and closed because it fails triangulation and does not support the feature_045 hypothesis. The interactions H169 and H172 are rejected and closed because they do not establish meaningful effect modification. Overall, the critical review does not reveal leakage or invalid Welch cells; all reported cells meet the minimum cell-size rule. The main threats are selection/multiplicity, winner's-curse attenuation, dependence among outcome and predictor screens, and the fact that these are observational comparisons only. Independent validation of H163 is therefore the most useful next evidence; a positive validation interval excluding null and exceeding the clinical threshold would make H163 acceptable as a dataset-specific association, while null, opposite, or subthreshold validation would close the feature_045 lead and leave the broad screen without robust accepted findings.",
 "research_notes": "Accepted set remains empty. The H138/H177 outcome_012 feature_034-feature_002 interaction screen is now closed: decomposition shows only small or opposite stratum contrasts, and validation did not give sufficient precision despite directional consistency. H174/H175 are null/opposite context contrasts and closed. The active residual candidate is H163, outcome_006 feature_045. It has a large discovery signed effect and coherent positive stratum contrasts under the negative direction (H167, H168, H170, H171), but all intervals remain imprecise and the outcome_014 triangulation H173 is opposite/null. Request validation for H163 only. If validation supports a clinically meaningful stronger-dependency effect, accept H163 as a dataset-specific association and revisit whether supporting stratum contrasts merit separate consideration. If validation is null, opposite, or below threshold, close H163 and all remaining feature_045 supporting contrasts. Do not validate already-validated H138 because cached evidence would not add information. Keep all claims observational, noncausal, and dataset-specific.",
